  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, and it passes `typecheck`. I haven't run `vite build` or looked at it in a browser, so none of the visuals are checked.\n\n- **Crystals:** eight hexagonal prisms with pointed tops, built as one custom mesh from `geometry.define`. Heights run from 0.7 to 2.3, and tilts and twists differ. Every triangle has its own vertices and a flat normal, and each face has its own colour, set as vertex colours on a `material.pbr` material.\n- **Rotation:** the cluster is a single node that turns slowly around the vertical axis. It sits on a two-tier cylinder pedestal.\n- **Sparks:** an additive-blend `effects.particles` emitter spawns small sparks over a disc under the cluster. A negative gravity makes them rise slowly, and a small noise value makes them drift.\n- **Look:** the background is near-black. Cyan and magenta directional lights from behind act as rim lights, with a dim front key light and a violet point light in the middle. Bloom is on. The rotation and the sparks make frames differ over time.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` and one more animation frame.\n\nThe particle settings (`shape: \"disc\"`, negative `gravity` for upward drift) come from the type definitions, not from a working example in the docs. If the sparks don't rise as intended in the browser, that is the first place to look.\n\n",
